        object: "ruling",
        oracle_id: "09f09d0a-6054-4545-b81e-0295773cc5f0",
        source: "wotc",
        published_at: "2026-06-29",
        comment: "If you cast an adventurer card as an Adventure, use only its alternative characteristics to determine whether it's legal to cast that spell. For example, if you control Gandalf, Party Guest (\"At the beginning of combat on your turn, you may cast an instant or sorcery spell with mana value X or less from your hand without paying its mana cost, where X is twice the number of legendary Wizards you control.\"), you could cast Burglar's Plot from your hand without paying its mana cost (provided you control enough legendary Wizards), but not Bilbo, Luckwearer.",
